## Third-party provenance

The manuals are **distillations written in our own words**, not reproductions.
Several of them distil sources that are not ours to relicense, and the
obligations travel with the material regardless of what this file says:

| Manual | Source | Terms |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 01–09 | *Imaginative Drawing* | All rights reserved. Principles distilled and chapters cited; nothing reproduced. |
| 10, 12 | George Bokhua, *Principles of Logo Design* | All rights reserved. Distilled and cited, never quoted at length. |
| 11 | Robin Williams, *The Non-Designer's Design Book*; Doyald Young, *Fonts and Logos* | All rights reserved. Same handling. |
| 12 §2.5 | *Graphic Design and Print Production Fundamentals* (BCcampus / Graphic Communications Open Textbook Collective) | **CC BY 4.0** — attributed in the manual. §2.4 of that book is CC BY-NC-ND 3.0 and is **not** adapted here. |
| 13 | `EpicInfographics` | MIT. Distilled with attribution. |

`docs/creative-sense-making.md` implements a framework from the research
literature — principally Nicholas Davis's work on creative sense-making and the
CCSM schema, cited in the document itself. Those papers are third-party and
mostly all-rights-reserved; the document distils and cites them and reproduces
none of them. `reference/` is third-party material, is not distributed with this
repository, and is covered by neither licence.

If you adapt a manual, CC BY-SA 4.0 requires you to share alike and to attribute
this project — and it does not relieve you of the obligations in the table above
for whatever those manuals distil.
